-- title:
--   The Burau representation is injective on the centre of the braid group
-- statement:
--   **The Burau representation is injective on the centre of the braid group.** Let $n$ be a natural number and $z \in Z(B_n)$ with $\rho_n(z) = I_n$; then $z = 1$. The centre $Z(B_n)$ is infinite cyclic generated by the full twist $\Delta_n^2$ (Chow 1948); the unreduced Burau representation sends $\Delta_n^2$ to the scalar matrix $t^{n(n-1)} I_n$ (equivalently, $\det \rho_n(\sigma_i) = -t$ and $\Delta_n^2$ has word length $n(n-1)$ in the Artin generators, so $\rho_n(\Delta_n^{2k}) = I_n$ forces $(-t)^{n(n-1)k} = 1$ in $\mathbb{Z}[t,t^{-1}]$, hence $k = 0$). This is the second structural input for Long's criterion: once $\ker \rho_n \le Z(B_n)$, injectivity on the centre kills the kernel.
-- source:
--   Standard facts: centre of B_n (Chow 1948); Burau image of the full twist. Structural input for Long's criterion (BurauFaithful.burau_faithful_of_faithful_on_normal, node 906aaa4a-93c6-4fbf-862e-71e93ea21242), arXiv:2607.05283v2.

import Definitions.Def_BurauFaithful_UnreducedBurau
set_option autoImplicit false

namespace BurauFaithful

theorem burau_injective_on_center (n : ℕ) (z : BraidsLinksMCG.ArtinBraidGroup n)
    (hz : z ∈ Subgroup.center (BraidsLinksMCG.ArtinBraidGroup n))
    (hρ : burauRep n z = 1) : z = 1 := by sorry

end BurauFaithful
